\f0\b\fs40 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
iScreenBar Menu Help\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa260\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 iScreenBar Menu keeps a BenQ iScreenBar lamp in step with an Apple Studio Display, and adds controls for the MacBook's built-in display and for keeping the Mac awake. It runs in the menu bar and has no Dock icon.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa248\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf0 Menu and control panel\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\fs26 \cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}Right-click
\f1\b0  (or Control-click) the menu bar icon for the menu: Light, Brightness, Color Temperature, Lamp modes, Ambient Rules, Displays, Favorites, Keep Awake, Control Panel\'85, Launch at Login, Help\'85, and Quit.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}Left-click
\f1\b0  the icon for the control panel. At the bottom right are 
\f0\b About\'85
\f1\b0 , 
\f0\b Help\'85
\f1\b0 , and 
\f0\b Quit
\f1\b0 .\
