\fs22 \cf2 Left-click: control panel  \'b7  Right-click: menu\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa260\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The menu and the panel share the same settings, so a change in one shows up in the other. A dimmed item isn't available right now, for example lamp items while the lamp is disconnected.\
The icon is yellow when the lamp is on, gray when it is off, and red when there is a problem. Hover over it to see the current brightness and color temperature.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa248\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf0 Quick Controls\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs26 \cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}Light
\f1\b0  turns the lamp on or off.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b {\listtext	\'95	}Auto Light
\f1\b0  lets the lamp's own sensor adjust the light. It can't be on at the same time as Match Screen.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b {\listtext	\'95	}Presence
\f1\b0  uses the lamp's presence detection. Set the away delay and sensitivity in the panel.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b {\listtext	\'95	}Video Mode
\f1\b0  turns on the lamp's video lighting mode.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b {\listtext	\'95	}Match Screen
\f1\b0 : set the lamp and the Studio Display to comfortable levels first, then turn this on. The lamp then follows the display's brightness, keeping that difference.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b {\listtext	\'95	}Sleep Sync
\f1\b0  turns the lamp off when the Studio Display sleeps, and back on when it wakes.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b {\listtext	\'95	}Wake Screen
\f1\b0  (switch next to the Presence Detection heading) wakes the sleeping Studio Display when you come back and presence detection turns the lamp on. It needs Presence and Sleep Sync. A locked Mac shows the lock screen. Someone passing within range can also wake it. The lamp must have been off for a minute first, so locking the Mac while you stay seated doesn't wake the display again.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b {\listtext	\'95	}Auto Temp
\f1\b0  changes color temperature with the time of day (cooler during the day, warmer at night). It doesn't measure the room.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b {\listtext	\'95	}Link Screens
\f1\b0  keeps the MacBook display and the Studio Display brightness in step.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}Keep Awake
\f1\b0  keeps the Mac awake (macOS asks for an administrator password). Turn it off when you're done. It is also released when you quit.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa248\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf0 Brightness and color temperature\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa260\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 The sliders show the values read back from the lamp. 1% is the lowest level, not off. To turn the lamp off, use Light. The menu offers quick steps: 25/50/75/100% and 2700/4000/5000/6500K.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa248\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf0 Ambient light calibration\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa260\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs26 \cf0 Click 
\f0\b Bright: Off
\f1\b0  when the room is bright enough without the lamp, and 
\f0\b Dim: On
\f1\b0  when you want extra light. Each saves the current Studio Display sensor reading. 
\f0\b Enable
\f1\b0  (or Ambient Rules in the menu) reuses the saved points.\
Changes aren't instant: turning off, or turning on quickly, needs about 30 seconds of steady readings, and the gradual turn-on takes about 45 seconds. Sleep Sync wins: a dark room doesn't turn the lamp on while the display is asleep.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa248\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf0 Displays and rotation\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\fs26 \cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}Built-in
\f1\b0  turns the MacBook's built-in display off or on. It can only be turned off while an external display is connected. If the Studio Display is unplugged, the built-in display is turned back on.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b {\listtext	\'95	}Rotate
\f1\b0  changes the built-in display's rotation. If you don't confirm within 5 seconds, it reverts.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b {\listtext	\'95	}Studio Display
\f1\b0  covers the screen with a black overlay. Windows stay where they are, but the backlight stays on. Double-click the black screen or turn the switch back on to restore it.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\'95	}A 
\f0\b rotation preset
\f1\b0  saves the built-in display's on/off state, rotation, and main-display role. With Enable Preset on, it is applied whenever the Studio Display connects. Turning it off returns the built-in display to 0\'b0. On a Mac with no built-in display and only the Studio Display, this section and the rotation preset are hidden; Studio Display stays in the menu under Displays.\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\sb80\sa40\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
